    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "A rectangle has length $\\frac{2x}{3}$ m and width $\\frac{3x}{4}$ m. What is the area of the rectangle? Find the area if $x=12$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac{x^2}{2}\\text{ m}^2$; $72\\text{ m}^2$.",
      "worked": "Using $A=lw$:\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=\\frac{2x}{3}\\times\\frac{3x}{4}\\\\A&=\\frac{6x^2}{12}\\\\A&=\\frac{x^2}{2}\\text{ m}^2\\end{align*}$$\nWhen $x=12$:\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=\\frac{12^2}{2}\\\\A&=\\frac{144}{2}\\\\A&=72\\text{ m}^2\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 52
  },
